  "reason": "We have an image-only baseline (config_011: 22.7% acc) and a multimodal result (config_004: 53.7% acc), but no RNA-only baseline. This large gap tells us RNA contributes substantially, but we cannot yet determine whether the multimodal fusion is genuinely additive or whether RNA alone would already achieve ~50%+. Config_023 (rna_only, singleprofile, scvi_n200) is a clean single-modality experiment using the same RNA encoder and profile setting as our best multimodal result, making it a controlled complement to config_011. Together, these two single-modality baselines bracket the multimodal result and reveal whether the 53.7% reflects true cross-modal synergy or is dominated by RNA. This is the most decision-relevant uncertainty to resolve next: if RNA alone is already ~50%, we should focus budget on RNA representation improvements rather than multimodal fusion complexity; if RNA alone is much lower, the multimodal combination is genuinely valuable and we should invest in optimizing fusion and image encoders. No other single experiment would reduce this foundational uncertainty as efficiently."
}

